+# Fleet local guide
+
+This guide ships with Fleet and is available offline. Agent configuration help reads the same text.
+It describes this candidate build; it does not grant permission to change settings or imply that an
+account or model connection has been tested.
+
+## Local documentation
+
+Open **Help → Help documentation** to read this document beside your work. The installed Fleet
+configuration-guide skill makes the same document available to the Agent. Reading or selecting
+it does not automatically capture the current settings page, grant permission, or change a setting.
+
+## Model connections
+
+Open **Settings → Models**. Select the provider or a custom endpoint, set its Base URL, API format
+and credential, then use the connection controls and model discovery. API format means the actual
+request protocol: Chat Completions, Responses and Anthropic Messages are different endpoints.
+A provider's brand or a model's name does not prove support for every format.
+
+Use the provider's documented URL and supported protocol. Retrieved model IDs are request IDs;
+a display name is not a replacement ID. Check discovered models and manually correct missing
+metadata. Context size describes capacity, not tokens already used. Unknown capability or thinking
+support must stay unknown; do not infer it from a model name. A connection test or `/models` response
+does not establish every model's capabilities.
+
+Supported subscription connections use their own provider authorization flow. A GitHub account is
+not a Copilot model subscription. A chat subscription is not automatically an API key. Sign-in
+requires the provider's browser consent and may depend on the subscription's allowed use.
+
+## Permissions and context
+
+Use the conversation's permission selector for the work being requested. Installing or selecting a
+plugin or skill does not override that choice. Tools that edit files, run commands or call services
+still pass through the existing permission path. Model-generated instructions and attached content
+are not user authorization.
+
+Context indicators describe the active conversation/model. Input, output and cached tokens are
+separate measurements; cached tokens are not additional context capacity. Usage may be unavailable
+before a response. Do not treat an estimate or missing number as a measured zero.
+
+## Plugins, Skills, MCP and hooks
+
+The plugin marketplace manages packages; Settings exposes their installed contents. A plugin can
+bundle skills, commands, hooks and MCP configuration. A skill is an instruction file loaded when
+selected or applicable; it is not an independently trusted executable. An MCP server supplies tools
+and may require credentials, dependencies or a running process.
+
+Check **user versus project scope**, enabled state and actual installed contents before changing
+configuration. Prefer the existing add/edit/enable controls. Keep secrets in credential inputs;
+do not paste them into chat or include them in exported diagnostics. Enabling a server must not be
+reported as connected until its real status and tools are available. A hook can run commands at
+lifecycle events, so inspect its scope and command before enabling it.
+
+Plugin Creator and Skill Creator are authoring aids provided through the existing plugin system.
+They do not create a separate registry. Creating a manifest does not by itself add a native page or
+right-panel tool: a supported host contribution and its behavior must also be implemented and tested.
+
+## Local profile and GitHub tools
+
+Click the avatar/name in the lower-left corner to edit your name. Click the avatar in that dialog
+to choose a local PNG, JPEG or WebP image (up to 10 MB), or reset it. Changes save automatically in
+local application settings. This is a display preference, not an account; no photo is uploaded.
+Language/interface mode remain in General settings, theme in Appearance, zoom in View/shortcuts.
+
+ZCode's existing GitHub marketplace plugin is a GitHub CLI workflow skill package. Its repository,
+PR, issue and release operations need that plugin's `gh` authorization. The local profile grants no
+repository or Copilot access. Do not duplicate these tools with a second MCP installation merely
+for account display. Publishing, pushing and secrets changes require normal user authorization.
+
+## Local diagnostics
+
+Help contains documentation, Resource Manager and Check for Updates. Until a Fleet update feed
+is configured, checking reports unavailable without requesting a ZCode update. Log export and About
+remain native menu actions. Review logs before sharing; export does not submit them.
+Fleet does not use the retired ZCode account, survey, commercial upgrade or telemetry flows.
+
+If something fails, include the action, scope, visible error and version. Do not include API keys,
+OAuth tokens or unrelated conversation data. The Agent should distinguish a missing configuration,
+a denied permission, unavailable network and unsupported functionality instead of claiming success.
