+---
+name: fleet-configuration-guide
+description: Read the packaged Fleet guide to explain or help configure model connections, permissions, plugins, Skills, MCP and GitHub. Use only when the user requests help with Fleet.
+---
+
+# Fleet configuration guide
+
+Read `../../docs/guide.en.md` (or `../../docs/guide.zh-CN.md` for Chinese). These are the same
+local documents the user sees in Help. Do not use a hosted ZCode guide as Fleet's authority.
+
+1. Establish the user's goal and the current user/project scope. Inspect the installed version,
+   existing settings and available configuration tools before proposing a change.
+2. Never guess a config path from a screenshot or from the old product name. Resolve the current
+   profile and the existing service/config schema. Preserve unknown keys and unrelated settings.
+3. Explain relevant choices in the user's language. A question is not permission to edit.
+   For an authorized edit, use the existing setting/plugin/MCP operation where available.
+   Do not create another credential store, Session database, plugin registry or permission route.
+4. Never request tokens in chat, print credentials, read the encrypted credential store directly,
+   copy another product's OAuth Client ID or bypass provider login consent.
+5. Follow the user's permission mode. Plugins and this guide grant no additional permission.
+   Do not enable a plugin, install dependencies, start external services, make paid model requests
+   or contact a remote service merely to explain a setting.
+6. Validate the resulting config and read back the affected public settings. Report unsupported
+   actions honestly. If an operation is not exposed, explain the limitation before suggesting a
+   scoped file edit. Do not invent tool names or successful connections.
+
+This skill is loaded through the ordinary plugin/skill mechanism. Disabling or uninstalling the
+plugin must remain effective. Help may still display packaged reference documents offline.
